prompt:
Build ONE self-contained HTML file: a 2D side-view simulation of a bridge DECK segment rendered on <canvas data-testid="simulation">. Physics (this is what gets graded): the deck is a chain of N = 11 point masses (nodes 0..10), 1000 kg each, spaced 10 m apart in a straight horizontal line at height y = 0 (y axis points UP, gravity g = 9.81 pulls -y). Adjacent nodes are linked by spring-damper elements: stiffness k = 8e6 N/m, damping c = 8e4 N-s/m, rest length 10 m. Additionally every free node feels global air damping of 2000 N-s/m opposing its velocity (this settles the span in seconds; it does not affect the static sag). Nodes 0 and 10 are PINNED (fixed position forever). All other nodes move under gravity plus spring forces, integrated with semi-implicit (symplectic) Euler at a FIXED timestep dt = 0.001 s. A link BREAKS when its length exceeds 11.5 m (15% strain); broken links exert no force. collapsed = true if any link is broken. maxSag = max over nodes of (0 - y), i.e. downward displacement in meters, positive down. Draw the deck, the two pinned abutments, plus two towers and a main cable with hangers as decoration (visual only — they carry no load in this model), a live readout of maxSag, and turn broken links red.

MANDATORY benchmark API — a hidden automated grader calls exactly this; it must exist on window before load finishes, be deterministic for a given seed, and be independent of wall-clock time:
window.BENCH = {
  reset(seed) {},              // all nodes back on the straight line at rest; seed accepted and stored (same seed => same run; add only a deterministic sub-micron perturbation derived from seed)
  step(ms) {},                 // advance physics by exactly ms milliseconds of simulated time using fixed 1 ms substeps
  perform(action, payload) {}, // 'load' with payload {node: 0..10, kg: number} adds that many kg of static mass to the node (accumulates until reset)
  getState() { return {seed, timeMs, collapsed}; },
  getMetrics() { return {timeMs, centerY, maxSag}; }
};
centerY = y position (meters, y-up) of node 5. Include <button data-testid="reset">Reset</button> wired to BENCH.reset(1). The scene must also animate via requestAnimationFrame during free viewing. No external libraries — plain canvas 2D and vanilla JS only.
